#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296534 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c7d07e0-64af-5e75-ad82-b431a24dc3ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296536} {:answer/id #uuid "e606dc4f-085c-5e0f-b9d4-f76e42f7530b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{6}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296537} {:answer/id #uuid "843a71ca-2a37-5f1d-b88f-0fe4cbccab94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296538} {:answer/id #uuid "5fd91e00-f071-5e2b-a35f-7dfb3e834f76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296539} {:answer/id #uuid "34f667e6-631b-5dec-928c-e51036c02907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "843a71ca-2a37-5f1d-b88f-0fe4cbccab94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296538} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3543fc8-4567-5400-b13e-4f0ddcc3363c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296535}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9f02eae8-3929-554e-892f-cc66f87ecf6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-114309" :question/problem "$\\int (x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x+4\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x+4)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(x+4)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064399 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88348853-a5ed-56e7-b188-38b7a12b3d8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)\\sin(3x)}9+\\frac{\\cos(3x)}3+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061079} {:answer/id #uuid "a5cd278f-7ff3-5ea7-b04c-b6e663b16d24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)\\sin(3x)}3+\\frac{\\cos(3x)}9+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061080} {:answer/id #uuid "0cff53e8-8b89-5d94-97d4-0c33b18efe9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sin(3x)}3+\\frac{x\\cos(3x)}9+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061081} {:answer/id #uuid "1b3ba8eb-336f-58ec-a6c0-aa2eb27db70c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)\\sin(3x)}3-\\frac{x\\cos(3x)}3+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061082} {:answer/id #uuid "5a740846-615a-5a3c-b19a-b243c8b63163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\sin(3x)}9+\\frac{\\cos(3x)}3+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5cd278f-7ff3-5ea7-b04c-b6e663b16d24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)\\sin(3x)}3+\\frac{\\cos(3x)}9+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061080} :answer-field/id #uuid "9942d92f-0c37-50cf-9a06-af63bbead44f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f405e14-26e8-524b-b2bf-2f3fef1fc543" :question/math-academy-id "q-12564" :question/problem "$\\int (x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x+3\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x+3)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(x+3)\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289161 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ecd12ba-ead6-5c9b-8b19-d74505a582ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289163} {:answer/id #uuid "063f1038-b031-50a8-9960-e1cfd90959d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289164} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b17332-732c-555e-b0f4-f4f78b98b353" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289165} {:answer/id #uuid "48db7a12-5f2d-570a-af53-80aeae1b7bc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289166} {:answer/id #uuid "a3040a83-50d0-52cd-83d6-0701b7b0b560" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4b17332-732c-555e-b0f4-f4f78b98b353" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289165} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca396769-eb6d-53cf-8398-a4cc0df729e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39c1f4f6-a031-555a-af2e-76dd70b7318e" :question/math-academy-id "q-14453" :question/problem "$\\int 6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))+C \\\\  & =6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351885 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b921defa-1211-5826-a8e9-e8b187eee7f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}e^4+\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b921defa-1211-5826-a8e9-e8b187eee7f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}e^4+\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351887} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f50aba1-c314-5a83-8359-d16e3fe2c6a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24fe0b51-6352-5f7d-ac11-80fbb39fffe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-349217" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}3x{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{2x} & ⇒ & v=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}-\\int \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3x{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}x{e}^{2x}\\,{|}_{0}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}x{e}^{2x}\\,{|}_{0}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2x}\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(2\\cdot {e}^{4}-0\\cdot {e}^{0})-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{4}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{4}-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{4}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{9{e}^{4}+3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289178 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Definite Integral Using Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47159201-f331-5c83-8ddc-383828eab39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1-{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289180} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec45187-f1eb-5762-bc52-0346ef62c508" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2-{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289181} {:answer/id #uuid "79884932-1291-545f-9074-499a42fc8d05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289182} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c8873c-e846-535c-974e-1e7cb0f4edec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-3{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289183} {:answer/id #uuid "e70e8dbd-5827-511d-a205-b64b96acb6b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1+{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47159201-f331-5c83-8ddc-383828eab39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1-{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289180} :answer-field/id #uuid "194e6f4a-2d92-5da0-9dac-d53c5bf8c3a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f7920756-127c-56a7-b85e-2c3d28bb75c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-49660" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-2}^{0}x{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-x} & ⇒ & v=-{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (-{e}^{-x})-\\int (-{e}^{-x})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}x{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-x{e}^{-x}{|}_{-2}^{0}+{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x{e}^{-x}{|}_{-2}^{0}-{e}^{-x}{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =[-0{e}^{-0}-2{e}^{2}]-[{e}^{0}-{e}^{2}] \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2}-1+{e}^{2} \\\\  & =-1-{e}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
